WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.200
Sixteen defects, all found by reading.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.200
Nothing asserts any of them.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.400
So freeze the pages themselves.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.900
Write down what each one must yield.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.000
It runs on every pull request.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
No model, no network, no GPU.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.200
Then put five old defects back.

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.900
Four of five. The fifth, honestly, no.

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.100
And a tenth page read as empty.

10
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.600
Two dozen releases. No dates found.

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.600
The same date, written twice.

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.000
The rule read the second as prose.

13
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.600
Step over it: 24 of 24.

14
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.100
And the subjects are real pages now.

15
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.600
Build the instrument. It finds the next one.
